Summary
=======

Problem:
Attackers could introduce Rogue DHCP Servers and provide false network settings.

Solution:
DHCP Snooping allows only trusted DHCP Servers to send DHCP responses.

Benefit:
Prevents Rogue DHCP attacks and creates a trusted IP-MAC binding database.

Limitation:
Does not stop ARP Spoofing attacks.

